description:
**What:** Critical correctness bug. In crate-jmap-contacts-server/src/addressbook.rs handle_address_book_set, the post-set block matches Some(Value::Object(is_default_map)) and iterates it as a map. The spec (draft-ietf-jmap-contacts-10 §2.3) defines onSuccessSetIsDefault as Id|null — a single string id, not a map. Also fix the incorrect doc-comment on the field.

**Algorithm:**
1. Replace the post-set block (currently iterating a map) with:
   match on_success_set_is_default {
       Some(Value::String(id_str)) => {
           // resolve creation reference: if id_str starts with '#', look up in created map
           let resolved: Option<Id> = if id_str.starts_with('#') {
               created.get(&id_str[1..]).and_then(|v| v.get("id")).and_then(|v| v.as_str()).map(Id::from)
           } else {
               Some(Id::from(id_str.as_str()))
           };
           if let Some(target_id) = resolved {
               let patch = json!({"isDefault": true});
               match backend.update_object::<AddressBook>(&account_id, &target_id, patch).await {
                   Ok(Some(obj)) => { updated.insert(target_id.to_string(), ...); mutated = true; }
                   Ok(None) => {}  // silently ignored per §2.3
                   Err(_) => {}    // silently ignored per §2.3
               }
           }
       }
       Some(Value::Null) | None => {}
       _ => {}  // malformed — ignore
   }
2. Correct the doc-comment on AddressBookSetParams.on_success_set_is_default to say Id|null (single id string), not a map.
3. Add test set_on_success_set_is_default_bare_id: pass as a string id; assert target book appears in updated.
4. Add test set_on_success_set_is_default_bad_id_ignored: pass non-existent id; assert no error returned, notUpdated empty. Oracle: §2.3 must be ignored.
5. cargo test -p jmap-contacts-server.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- onSuccessSetIsDefault accepts a bare string Id, not a JSON object.
- Creation reference #c1 resolved to server-assigned id.
- Non-existent id silently ignored per §2.3.
- Doc-comment corrected.
- cargo test -p jmap-contacts-server exits 0.
